1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,301
That brown or orange ring in your toilet

2
00:00:02,311 --> 00:00:05,653
bowl won't go away, no matter how much you
brush.

3
00:00:06,014 --> 00:00:09,359
It's not dirt, it's hard water minerals,
and

4
00:00:09,369 --> 00:00:11,621
ordinary cleaners barely touch it.

5
00:00:12,074 --> 00:00:14,827
In seven steps, you'll learn the simple
method

6
00:00:14,837 --> 00:00:19,004
that dissolves the ring, using ingredients
you may already own.

7
00:00:19,551 --> 00:00:22,339
It works on rust-colored rings too, and
I'll

8
00:00:22,349 --> 00:00:24,809
show you what to do if the stain won't
budge.

9
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:26,483
WikiTube.

10
00:00:26,774 --> 00:00:29,060
Whatever it is, here's how.

11
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:32,281
Toilet rings form where the water line
sits.

12
00:00:32,642 --> 00:00:36,510
Minerals like calcium, magnesium and iron
settle on

13
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:39,818
the porcelain and harden over time, and
bacteria

14
00:00:39,828 --> 00:00:41,302
love the rough surface.

15
00:00:41,663 --> 00:00:43,926
A normal brush glides over them.

16
00:00:44,728 --> 00:00:47,493
What works is an acidic cleaner that
dissolves

17
00:00:47,503 --> 00:00:50,973
the minerals, plus a little patience while
it soaks.

18
00:00:51,938 --> 00:00:54,796
Before we begin, one safety rule you must

19
00:00:54,806 --> 00:00:58,894
remember: never mix cleaning products,
especially

20
00:00:58,904 --> 00:01:01,306
bleach with vinegar or any acid.

21
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:04,107
The method takes about ten minutes of your

22
00:01:04,117 --> 00:01:06,775
time, and the rest is waiting.

23
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:08,505
Here's what you need.

24
00:01:08,796 --> 00:01:12,258
Plain white vinegar, or citric acid
powder, which

25
00:01:12,268 --> 00:01:14,775
is stronger and still gentle on porcelain.

26
00:01:15,066 --> 00:01:16,145
Rubber gloves.

27
00:01:16,378 --> 00:01:17,584
A toilet brush.

28
00:01:17,817 --> 00:01:21,009
A pumice stone, only for stubborn rings.

29
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:24,527
And a window or a fan, for fresh air.

30
00:01:25,329 --> 00:01:28,396
That's all, and please keep every bleach
product

31
00:01:28,406 --> 00:01:30,146
far away from this job.

32
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:34,279
A small amount of patience is the only
other ingredient.

33
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:35,819
Step one.

34
00:01:36,273 --> 00:01:38,643
Open a window or turn on the bathroom

35
00:01:38,653 --> 00:01:41,334
fan, and put on rubber gloves.

36
00:01:41,695 --> 00:01:44,390
Before you start, make sure that no bleach

37
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,515
or bleach-based cleaner has been used in
the

38
00:01:46,525 --> 00:01:50,067
bowl recently, because bleach and acids,
such as

39
00:01:50,077 --> 00:01:54,744
vinegar or citric acid, create dangerous
fumes when they meet.

40
00:01:55,290 --> 00:01:57,707
If you used bleach or any toilet cleaner

41
00:01:57,717 --> 00:02:00,583
today, flush twice and wait.

42
00:02:01,385 --> 00:02:03,314
We will only use one product at a

43
00:02:03,324 --> 00:02:06,330
time, and we will rinse thoroughly in
between.

44
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:08,245
Safety first.

45
00:02:08,792 --> 00:02:11,023
Keep children and pets out of the bathroom

46
00:02:11,033 --> 00:02:13,667
while you work, just to be safe.

47
00:02:14,233 --> 00:02:15,265
Step two.

48
00:02:16,067 --> 00:02:18,576
The ring sits at the waterline, and the

49
00:02:18,586 --> 00:02:21,325
water in the bowl dilutes your cleaner.

50
00:02:21,988 --> 00:02:25,029
To expose the ring, lower the water level.

51
00:02:25,483 --> 00:02:28,222
Turn off the water valve behind the
toilet,

52
00:02:28,316 --> 00:02:32,784
flush, and the tank empties, leaving the
bowl low.

53
00:02:33,586 --> 00:02:35,573
Or use your brush to push the water

54
00:02:35,583 --> 00:02:38,580
down the drain, then remove the water left

55
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:39,483
in the bowl.

56
00:02:40,146 --> 00:02:42,433
Even a lower level helps a lot.

57
00:02:43,583 --> 00:02:46,485
Now the cleaner can touch the stain
directly,

58
00:02:46,509 --> 00:02:48,899
which is the real secret of this method.

59
00:02:49,864 --> 00:02:51,955
If your toilet has a very small amount

60
00:02:51,965 --> 00:02:54,461
of water, this step is easy.

61
00:02:55,007 --> 00:02:57,633
Don't worry about being perfect, since a
lower

62
00:02:57,643 --> 00:02:59,105
level is enough.

63
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:00,688
Step three.

64
00:03:01,049 --> 00:03:03,581
Pour about two cups of white vinegar
around

65
00:03:03,591 --> 00:03:05,717
the bowl so it coats the ring all

66
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:06,690
the way round.

67
00:03:07,655 --> 00:03:10,988
For a stronger option, dissolve three
tablespoons of

68
00:03:10,998 --> 00:03:13,459
citric acid in a cup of hot water,

69
00:03:13,483 --> 00:03:15,154
and pour it on the stain.

70
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:19,403
Both are acids that dissolve limescale and
rust.

71
00:03:20,368 --> 00:03:23,260
For a vertical stain, soak some toilet
paper

72
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:25,419
in the vinegar and press it against the

73
00:03:25,429 --> 00:03:27,948
ring, so it stays in contact.

74
00:03:29,098 --> 00:03:31,433
Let it sit and do the work, without

75
00:03:31,443 --> 00:03:32,836
any scrubbing for now.

76
00:03:33,196 --> 00:03:35,474
A funnel or a small cup helps you

77
00:03:35,484 --> 00:03:38,353
pour precisely, so the liquid doesn't
splash on

78
00:03:38,363 --> 00:03:40,220
the seat or on the floor.

79
00:03:40,767 --> 00:03:41,788
Step four.

80
00:03:42,149 --> 00:03:44,203
Wait at least thirty minutes.

81
00:03:45,353 --> 00:03:47,967
For tough, old rings, leave it for two

82
00:03:47,977 --> 00:03:51,578
hours, or even overnight, with the lid
closed

83
00:03:51,588 --> 00:03:53,503
so nobody uses the toilet.

84
00:03:53,794 --> 00:03:56,940
The acid needs time to soften the mineral
layer.

85
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,923
This is the step that replaces hard
scrubbing,

86
00:04:00,052 --> 00:04:01,305
so don't rush it.

87
00:04:01,851 --> 00:04:03,989
If your bathroom is shared, put a note

88
00:04:03,999 --> 00:04:04,834
on the lid.

89
00:04:05,799 --> 00:04:08,111
During the wait, you can wipe the outside

90
00:04:08,121 --> 00:04:10,293
of the toilet, the seat and the handle

91
00:04:10,303 --> 00:04:13,727
with a cloth and warm soapy water, then
rinse.

92
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:16,793
Close the bathroom door while it works.

93
00:04:17,153 --> 00:04:20,057
Give the acid a chance, because patience
here

94
00:04:20,067 --> 00:04:22,249
replaces elbow grease later.

95
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,937
Step five.

96
00:04:24,391 --> 00:04:27,283
After the soak, take your toilet brush and

97
00:04:27,293 --> 00:04:30,438
scrub the ring in firm, circular motions.

98
00:04:30,730 --> 00:04:33,352
You'll find the ring is much softer now,

99
00:04:33,377 --> 00:04:36,127
and it should lift off with far less
effort.

100
00:04:36,488 --> 00:04:40,388
Brush under the rim too, because minerals
gather there.

101
00:04:40,749 --> 00:04:43,200
If any of the ring remains, repeat the

102
00:04:43,210 --> 00:04:46,042
vinegar or citric acid soak once more.

103
00:04:46,705 --> 00:04:49,281
Don't use a wire brush or steel wool,

104
00:04:49,305 --> 00:04:51,756
which can scratch the porcelain and make
future

105
00:04:51,766 --> 00:04:53,913
stains stick even faster.

106
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:57,329
Always wear gloves, and be careful not to

107
00:04:57,339 --> 00:04:58,534
splash the water.

108
00:04:59,499 --> 00:05:01,680
Work from the top of the bowl down,

109
00:05:01,705 --> 00:05:03,724
and rinse your brush afterward.

110
00:05:04,267 --> 00:05:05,288
Step six.

111
00:05:05,579 --> 00:05:07,822
For rings that won't budge, use a pumice

112
00:05:07,832 --> 00:05:10,536
stone, but only on white porcelain.

113
00:05:10,897 --> 00:05:13,882
Wet the stone and the stain thoroughly,
and

114
00:05:13,892 --> 00:05:16,645
keep both wet the whole time, because a

115
00:05:16,655 --> 00:05:18,477
dry stone scratches.

116
00:05:19,024 --> 00:05:22,195
Rub with very light pressure, and use
short

117
00:05:22,205 --> 00:05:25,002
strokes, until the stain comes off.

118
00:05:25,293 --> 00:05:27,278
Then rinse and check.

119
00:05:28,242 --> 00:05:31,424
Don't use pumice on plastic, colored or
glazed

120
00:05:31,434 --> 00:05:33,152
surfaces that are damaged.

121
00:05:33,606 --> 00:05:36,370
If you are unsure, test in a small

122
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:37,970
hidden spot first.

123
00:05:38,424 --> 00:05:41,755
This tool removes the last bit of stubborn
mineral.

124
00:05:42,905 --> 00:05:46,259
Don't press hard, because the stone should
do the work.

125
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:49,510
Stop if you see any scratches on the
surface.

126
00:05:50,067 --> 00:05:51,111
Step seven.

127
00:05:51,658 --> 00:05:54,225
Turn the water valve back on, let the

128
00:05:54,235 --> 00:05:58,321
tank refill, and flush two or three times
to rinse.

129
00:05:58,867 --> 00:06:00,863
Admire the clean porcelain.

130
00:06:01,317 --> 00:06:03,676
To keep the ring from returning, brush the

131
00:06:03,686 --> 00:06:06,601
bowl weekly, and once a week, pour a

132
00:06:06,611 --> 00:06:09,005
cup of vinegar into the bowl and let

133
00:06:09,015 --> 00:06:11,684
it sit for an hour before flushing.

134
00:06:12,347 --> 00:06:14,856
If you have very hard water, consider a

135
00:06:14,866 --> 00:06:18,244
water softener, or an in-tank descaler.

136
00:06:18,906 --> 00:06:21,346
A few minutes of weekly care beats an

137
00:06:21,356 --> 00:06:23,097
hour of hard work later.

138
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,897
A clean bowl is also easier to keep

139
00:06:25,907 --> 00:06:29,970
fresh, and makes any future cleaning quick
and simple.

140
00:06:30,533 --> 00:06:33,530
If the stain survived two soaks, look
closer

141
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:34,561
at what it is.

142
00:06:34,922 --> 00:06:37,628
A pink or orange slimy film that wipes

143
00:06:37,638 --> 00:06:40,331
off easily is not hard water at all.

144
00:06:40,877 --> 00:06:44,223
It is bacterial growth, and an ordinary
toilet

145
00:06:44,233 --> 00:06:45,521
cleaner handles it.

146
00:06:45,974 --> 00:06:48,008
A ring that returns a few days after

147
00:06:48,018 --> 00:06:50,631
you remove it points to minerals or iron

148
00:06:50,641 --> 00:06:51,593
in your water.

149
00:06:52,743 --> 00:06:55,110
Then repeat the soak on a schedule.

150
00:06:55,667 --> 00:06:59,509
To stop fighting the ring, deal with the
water itself.

151
00:07:00,474 --> 00:07:02,752
Your water utility can tell you how hard

152
00:07:02,762 --> 00:07:05,341
your supply is, and a cheap test kit

153
00:07:05,351 --> 00:07:06,487
does the same.

154
00:07:07,034 --> 00:07:08,940
If a stain trail runs from under the

155
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:11,413
rim or down to the drain, the tank

156
00:07:11,423 --> 00:07:13,837
may be leaking slowly into the bowl.

157
00:07:14,197 --> 00:07:17,459
A plumber can also advise you about a
water softener.

158
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,610
A few small habits make rings much less
likely.

159
00:07:21,971 --> 00:07:24,454
Do not drop bleach tablets into the tank.

160
00:07:24,745 --> 00:07:27,185
They damage the rubber parts, and they
should

161
00:07:27,195 --> 00:07:29,597
never meet vinegar or citric acid.

162
00:07:30,051 --> 00:07:32,688
Flush a spare toilet once a week, because

163
00:07:32,698 --> 00:07:35,402
water that sits still is where rings form.

164
00:07:36,367 --> 00:07:39,213
Brush the bowl after cleaning the
bathroom, while

165
00:07:39,223 --> 00:07:41,370
any stain is still thin.

166
00:07:41,933 --> 00:07:43,754
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

167
00:07:44,208 --> 00:07:48,610
First, and most important, never

168
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,465
mix cleaning products.

169
00:07:50,756 --> 00:07:54,425
Bleach with vinegar or ammonia makes toxic
gas.

170
00:07:55,389 --> 00:07:59,080
Second, don't scrub aggressively with
abrasive tools.

171
00:07:59,534 --> 00:08:03,933
They scratch the porcelain, and scratches
collect even more stains.

172
00:08:04,294 --> 00:08:07,230
And third, don't give up after ten
minutes.

173
00:08:07,684 --> 00:08:09,692
These minerals need time.

174
00:08:10,354 --> 00:08:12,562
Let the acid soak and do the hard

175
00:08:12,572 --> 00:08:15,276
work for you, then finish with a brush.

176
00:08:15,823 --> 00:08:18,007
If a stain does not move after two

177
00:08:18,017 --> 00:08:21,188
soaks, it may be rust, which needs a

178
00:08:21,198 --> 00:08:22,904
dedicated rust remover.

179
00:08:23,567 --> 00:08:25,551
Follow its label carefully.

180
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:27,190
Let's recap.

181
00:08:28,155 --> 00:08:32,031
Ventilate, put on gloves and never mix
products.

182
00:08:32,996 --> 00:08:34,341
Lower the water level.

183
00:08:34,702 --> 00:08:37,035
Apply vinegar or citric acid.

184
00:08:37,999 --> 00:08:39,032
Let it soak.

185
00:08:39,578 --> 00:08:40,878
Brush gently.

186
00:08:41,424 --> 00:08:44,280
Use a wet pumice stone on the stubborn
parts.

187
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:48,204
And rinse, then prevent the ring with a
weekly routine.

188
00:08:49,354 --> 00:08:52,514
Seven steps, mostly waiting, and a toilet
bowl

189
00:08:52,524 --> 00:08:53,869
that looks new again.

190
00:08:54,323 --> 00:08:56,542
If the ring stays, work out what it

191
00:08:56,552 --> 00:08:58,804
is, then fix the cause.

192
00:08:59,367 --> 00:09:01,981
That's how you remove toilet rings and
hard

193
00:09:01,991 --> 00:09:04,335
water stains without hard scrubbing.

194
00:09:04,696 --> 00:09:07,391
If your bowl is sparkling now, subscribe
to

195
00:09:07,401 --> 00:09:11,916
WikiTube, because we publish a new how-to
every single day.

196
00:09:12,463 --> 00:09:14,276
Tell us in the comments how bad your

197
00:09:14,286 --> 00:09:16,284
ring was, and what you would like us

198
00:09:16,294 --> 00:09:17,582
to explain next.

199
00:09:17,943 --> 00:09:19,161
See you tomorrow.

200
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:20,462
That's WikiTube.

201
00:09:20,695 --> 00:09:22,900
Whatever it is, here's how.
